                <pb facs="0504" n="1238" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1238"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-13"><hi rendition="#italic">March 13,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Consul Gibson reports that Americans at Marash, Hadjin, Aintab, Orfa apprehend
                    being massacred. A hostile feeling toward missionaries exists at Erzeroum, Van,
                    Bitlis. Have demanded telegraphic orders to all civil and military functionaries
                    to enforce respect for Americans, which I am informed at the Sublime Porte have
                    been sent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
